\title{Production system}
\taxon{Definition}
\date{2026-11-24}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{A \em{production system} is a forward chaining reasoning architecture that maintains an ongoing and constantly changing memory of factual assertions known as its \em{working memory} (WM) along with a collection of static and pre-imposed rules of the form #{A \subset C}, where #{A} is a condition on the current state of WM and #{C} is a resulting modification to the WM.}
